<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="592825c7">The environment plan can be a simple Excel spreadsheet containing information, such as the type of environment used, the
allocated hardware and its configuration, and dates. Alternatively, the environment plan can also be as detailed as a
project plan for more complex projects.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="f6e2d885"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e21774e2"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="878e1422"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="32e5852e">To serve as the coordination documentation and as a reference for the construction of an environment for all parties
involved.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="c1e4a71f">By not having an environment plan, it will be hard for IT personnel and the project team to coordinate their dependent
activities.</attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="5851b8ed">&lt;p&gt;
    This may not be needed if there is an existing environment in place.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
